Pixelado cores
==============

The engines Pixelado Party runs to play games, each one a program of its own. Distributed under the
GNU General Public License v3 (LICENSE). The changes are the patches and scripts in this repository,
made by Pixelado Dev from November 2026.

cores/nds/bananads/ (pixelado-core-bananads) is a modified version of BananaDS, itself built on melonDS:

- BananaDS: the bananads/ directory of SuperDrastic, https://github.com/JorreFog/SuperDrastic
  Copyright (c) 2026 JorreFog and contributors. GPLv3.
- melonDS: https://github.com/melonDS-emu/melonDS
  Copyright (c) Arisotura and the melonDS contributors. GPLv3.
- ENet (linked into the binary): Copyright (c) 2002-2024 Lee Salzman. MIT.
- cores/nds/bananads/build/apply-patches.sh: from Buildroot 2026.02.3, (c) 2002 Erik Andersen. GPLv2+.

cores/gba/gpsp/ (pixelado-core-gpsp) is gpSP built into this repository's own libretro frontend (retro/, common/):

- gpSP (gameplaySP): https://github.com/libretro/gpsp
  Copyright (c) 2006 Exophase, (c) 2021-2025 David Guillen Fandos, and the gpSP contributors.
  GPL-2.0-or-later (combined here under the GPL v3). It carries an open-source replacement for the GBA's BIOS,
  (c) 2002-2013 the VBA and VBA-M teams and Normmatt, GPL-2.0-or-later.
- libretro.h (retro/include/): Copyright (c) 2010-2020 The RetroArch team. MIT.

The DS binary is built with the Bootlin aarch64 glibc toolchain (stable-2025.08-1) and links the
console's glibc, libdrm and alsa-lib; libstdc++ and libgcc are linked in statically (GCC runtime
library exception).

The GBA binary is built with the same toolchain and links the console's glibc, libdrm and alsa-lib; libgcc is
linked in statically.

The cores contain no BIOS, firmware or games from Nintendo, and are not affiliated with Nintendo, BananaOS,
BananaDS, SuperDrastic, melonDS, gpSP or libretro. "Pixelado" and its logos are names of Pixelado Dev; the GPL
covers the code here, not the right to use those names for another product.
